# L §5.7 "Things have no order a rule can read ... first and last over things or movements take ties by (§5.11)";
# L §5.11 "Over things ... the ties by term is also the order first and last run in" (without one they are refused at
# load where load sees the binding: L5_11_first_no_ties_load; writer 8, sixth pass, round 18 C1-14, moved q1 there).
# q2: ties by lifespan(p).from: bo entered 2001, al 2005, so first is bo and last is al. q3: an ask's lines go in
# binding order, the text order of the things' stable ids persons:al < persons:bo (L §2.5), whatever their entry days.
# (Writer 8: was "ordered by the day they entered", removed by the review.)
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

kind persons

version a
  cite s
  known 2020-01-01
  persons + [bo] lives 2001-01-01..
  persons + [al] lives 2005-01-01..

ask q2: first(p in persons on 2026-01-01) ties by lifespan(p).from, last(p in persons on 2026-01-01) ties by lifespan(p).from
ask q3: lifespan(p).from for p in persons on 2026-01-01
=== expect
q2: (bo, al)
  cut 2026-01-01
q3 (p = al): 2005-01-01
  cut 2026-01-01
q3 (p = bo): 2001-01-01
  cut 2026-01-01
